VLA Forge

Third-party material and design credits.

1. SO-101 robot model (vendor/so101)
   From TheRobotStudio's SO-ARM100 repository, https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0. MJCF and STL meshes are used unmodified.

2. Wood texture (web/assets/wood_diff.jpg, wood_rough.jpg)
   "Wood Table 001" from Poly Haven, https://polyhaven.com, CC0.

3. three.js (web/vendor/three)
   https://threejs.org, MIT License.

4. Interface design
   The whole interface (shell, top bar, toolbar with segmented view tabs, side panels, prompt cards, composer,
   stage cards and dock, workplane grid, CSS tokens and motion) is ported from Etch, the author's own earlier
   project (deploy/etch-app at a0bb241d: editor.css, explore.css, new-board.css), with Etch's blue accent
   swapped for this page's safety orange (#ff5a1f).
   HeyPCB (https://heypcb.ai) was checked as a possible source and not used: its public repositories
   (github.com/HeyPCB) hold hardware designs under CERN-OHL-S-2.0, an MIT-licensed MCP server and KiCad
   boards, and no web interface code, so no HeyPCB code, name, logo or asset is in this project. HeyPCB is
   not affiliated with this project.

4a. Mascot
   The bot (web/mascot.js, eyes.js, spring.js, goo.js) is the character from Etch, the author's own earlier project
   (https://github.com/PranavAchar01/etch, deploy/etch-app at a0bb241d, live at https://etch-app-theta.vercel.app):
   js/ui/eyes.js (the eyes rig: states, activities, emotes, springs, blink and glance timers, gaze maths),
   js/ui/spring.js (spring physics), js/ui/goo.js (the gooey bubble) and the .ag-eyes rules of css/agent.css.
   The logic is carried over unchanged. The edits are marked "Meta:" in eyes.js: Meta blues for the body, smart
   glasses over the eyes and an infinity-loop antenna with a spring of its own. web/mascot.js plays the part of
   Etch's dock (js/ui/dock.js): it maps the page's events to the bot's states, emotes and bubbles. The earlier
   head-and-gripper bot drawn for this project was replaced by it.

5. Fonts
   Figtree and Averia Serif Libre (SIL Open Font License 1.1), loaded from Google Fonts, the same pair
   Etch uses. No other typeface.

6. Encoders
   facebook/dinov2-small (Apache-2.0) and google/siglip2-base-patch16-224 (Apache-2.0), loaded from the
   local Hugging Face cache.

7. Robot parts for the builder (vendor/menagerie)
   From MuJoCo Menagerie, https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie, commit
   98a70c569c4c1b6da467a20012f766ee1f8dc521, used unmodified, each folder with its upstream LICENSE:
   trs_so_arm100 (Apache-2.0), low_cost_robot_arm (Apache-2.0), trossen_wx250s and trossen_vx300s
   (BSD-3-Clause, Trossen Robotics), robotiq_2f85 (BSD-2-Clause, ROS-Industrial), franka_emika_panda hand.xml
   (Apache-2.0). Full table in SOURCES.md.

8. Factory line tote (vendor/robosuite)
   bins_arena.xml from robosuite, https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robosuite, commit
   5ce6643f3092639d08f7b0f90ed1c6a84f50552c, MIT License (Copyright (c) 2022 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab
   and UT Robot Perception and Learning Lab), kept unmodified with its LICENSE; bin1's collision boxes are
   scaled at run time (src/vla_forge/sim/line.py). The conveyor follows the construction given by MuJoCo's
   maintainers in google-deepmind/mujoco issue #547. Details in SOURCES.md.

9. Studio rendering (web/vendor/three)
   three.js r170 examples (MIT License, Copyright 2010-2024 three.js authors): RoomEnvironment, EffectComposer,
   RenderPass, GTAOPass, OutputPass, SMAAPass and their shaders. The robot meshes are unchanged (items 7 and 8);
   web/studio.js only assigns black and white materials and builds the lab floor, which is procedural
   (generated noise texture, no photograph or downloaded image).

10. Fixtures for the harder skills (src/vla_forge/sim/props.py)
   The kitting tray and the insertion socket are built in code from boxes: no downloaded mesh, no third-party
   asset, nothing to license. The parts are the forge's own 3 cm cubes.
